## Abilities and Tips

### P — Way of the Wanderer

Yasuo gains increased critical strike chance. He also generates Flow while moving, which creates a shield when fully charged and triggered by enemy champion or monster damage.

**How to use it:**
- Keep moving to charge your passive shield.
- Trade when your shield is available.
- Take advantage of critical strike items to reach your damage spikes.
- Wait for your shield to recharge before repeating dangerous trades.

**Common mistake:** Engaging without your shield and taking unnecessary damage.

### Q — Steel Tempest

Yasuo thrusts his sword forward, dealing physical damage. Hitting enemies generates Gathering Storm stacks. After two successful hits, his next Q launches a tornado that knocks enemies airborne.

Attack speed reduces Steel Tempest's cooldown and cast time, up to their limits.

**How to use it:**
- Use Q to last-hit minions and prepare tornadoes.
- Stack Q on minions before engaging.
- Combine E + Q for a circular attack.
- Use your tornado to enable Last Breath.

**Common mistake:** Throwing tornadoes immediately without predicting enemy movement.

### W — Wind Wall

Yasuo creates a wall that blocks many enemy projectiles.

**How to use it:**
- Save it for important enemy abilities.
- Protect teammates during teamfights.
- Position correctly around the wall.
- Learn which enemy abilities count as blockable projectiles.

**Common mistake:** Wasting Wind Wall on insignificant damage and having no protection against a crucial ability.

### E — Sweeping Blade

Yasuo dashes through a target, dealing magic damage. He cannot dash through the same target again for a short period.

**How to use it:**
- Use minions to approach or escape.
- Plan your dash targets before engaging.
- Combine E + Q for a circular strike.
- Preserve available minions for your escape.

**Common mistake:** Dashing automatically toward an enemy without considering your final position.

### R — Last Breath

Yasuo blinks to an airborne enemy champion, suspending airborne enemies and dealing physical damage. He restores his Flow and temporarily gains bonus armor penetration on critical strikes.

**How to use it:**
- Combine R with your tornado or allied knockups.
- Prioritize valuable airborne targets.
- Evaluate your landing position.
- Continue attacking after R to benefit from its armor penetration.

**Common mistake:** Ulting a tank and landing in the middle of the entire enemy team.

